                                "sense_id": "4e79fb88-dd20-31e7-bd9b-a8b24371ad21",
                                "text": "It had done well enough for a thousand years, it would do well enough still; it had stood firm against fierce sieges in the dark ages of the Roman baronry, it could afford to stand unchanged in its monumental strength against the advancing sea of nineteenth-century civilisation."
